] [17592186577292 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577281 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577292 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577308 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577292 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577292 1077 "III" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577292 1078 #edb/ref 17592186577281 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577292 1079 #uuid "51558782-e603-5130-857e-3b7d5a1aea98" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577293 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577314 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577293 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577328 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577293 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577293 1077 "I" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577293 1078 #edb/ref 17592186577328 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577293 1079 #uuid "54de8a04-1471-5f5a-8ae7-f7320ab59390" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577294 1068 #edb/ref 17592186577312 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577294 1068 #edb/ref 17592186577323 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577294 1068 #edb/ref 17592186577324 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577294 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577294 1071 "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}},\\qquad 3 x + 2>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577294 1072 #uuid "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577294 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)})/(-2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-\\ln(3 x + 2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577295 1080 "false" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577295 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577295 1083 #uuid "5ac82169-4017-5aee-b8a2-b79e679b0722" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577296 1080 "true" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577296 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577296 1083 #uuid "5f954ee0-b77e-54d7-9d1a-aeab4c66066f" 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577297 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577286 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577297 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577289 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577297 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139537008 17592186045443 true] [17592186577297 1077 "I" 1319413953